WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.630
The conflict in Ukraine is only one of the
wars Vladimir Putin is fighting.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.920
At home he’s cracked down viciously on dissent
and opposition.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.469
Putin’s chief target in Russia has been
this man – Alexei Navalny, now in jail with

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:18.779
his Anti-Corruption Foundation, banned and
labelled extremist.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:23.380
They’re calling on Russians to do whatever
they can to stop the war in Ukraine.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.060
But what about the dangers in taking on the
state?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:33.120
My guest this week in exile in London is one
of Navalny’s associates, Vladimir Ashurkov.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:44.390
"Organized opposition in Russia that can participate
in elections, that can launch campaigns, they

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:50.521
can-, that can do organized mass protests
– it's really not possible at this point.

00:00:50.521 --> 00:00:53.860
“
For now the group is naming and shaming thousands

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.610
of officials who’re supporting the war in
Ukraine – but how far will that dent Putin’s

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:00.610
power?

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:06.690
And why, despite so many common goals, are
Russian opposition groups still fighting amongst

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.520
themselves?

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:17.000
Vladimir Ashurkov, welcome to Conflict Zone.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.369
It's great to be with you.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:23.979
At the beginning of this month associates
of Alexei Navalny called for, what they put

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:29.640
it, as "a partisan underground” in Russia
to resist the war in Ukraine.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.790
Your organization is banned, it's labeled
extremist.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:38.289
So anybody who answers your call is taking
quite a risk, aren't they?

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:44.610
Let us put it into context: Throughout its
history Anti-Corruption Foundation and Alexei

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.030
Navalny team have been operating in Russia.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:54.070
At the peak of our activities we had a regional
network of branches in over 40 cities.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:58.719
We had about 200 people working for us in
Moscow.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:02:05.619
In spring of last year our organization has
been deemed extremist and we had to relocate

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.720
all the key people outside of Russia.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:20.940
Now, when the Russia started its brutal aggression
against Ukraine in February, even more restrictive

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.110
measures were put in place.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:31.209
At the same time, we are constantly monitoring
what goes on in Russia, in different regions.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:38.569
And over the last few months we have been
feeling that the discontent is growing and

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:46.370
our goal is to use our connection, our networks,
the people who used to work with us, our volunteers

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:52.040
to try to supplement this discontent and provide
some organizational structure.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.250
We created a...

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:56.640
Yes, but as you say they, as you say, times
have changed.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.159
Penalties have changed.

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:02.200
Your organization is no longer legal.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.239
It's on a par with Islamic State.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:09.519
It's been declared, you know, it's been declared
extremist.

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:13.760
You're asking people to spread information,
provide legal assistance.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:20.989
But also, and this is the most risky part,
sabotage the work of military enlistment centers.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:25.480
And the danger of getting caught doing that
is what?

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:31.299
There is danger in Russia now just for going
out to the street with a blank piece of paper

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:36.140
because the authorities assume you are protesting
against the war.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:42.459
At the same time, we encourage all Russian
people inside Russia, outside of Russia, to

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:50.709
do their part to stop this war and to bring
down this autocratic regime of Vladimir Putin.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:57.120
Everybody chooses what they do according to
their own abilities, according to their own

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:00.300
beliefs and appetite for risk.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:07.959
But to confront this regime is, I think, a
duty of any reasonable person.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:14.480
And we want to put the tools into the hands
of people who believe that they can do more

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:26.800
and who can do little bits and pieces, spread
out leaflets, in some cases sabotage, etc.,

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:27.800
etc.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.800
It's all...

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.450
Sabotage isn't bits and pieces, is it?

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.450
...clandestine activities...

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:32.580
Sabotage isn't bits and pieces.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.210
Sabotage is a pretty serious thing to get
engaged in.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:42.539
Yes, but it is our goal to bring down this
regime and sabotage is one of the non-violent

00:04:42.539 --> 00:04:44.110
instruments to do that.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:45.110
So we...

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.490
How is it nonviolent sabotage?

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:47.490
How is it nonviolent?

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.080
People have been blowing up enlistment centers,
haven't they?

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.280
Blowing up-, I've never-, I think you're mistaken.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.160
There has never been a blow up of an enlistment
center.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.160
There have been...

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.639
Alright, a fire started...

00:05:01.639 --> 00:05:09.639
There have been-, Starting fire to an enlistment
center that enlists people to fight in this

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:14.990
unfair and brutal war is, I think, is very
commendable.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:19.470
We definitely support this activity.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.680
And that's what we're doing.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:28.880
We created a system that allows people to
remain anonymous, so we try as much as possible

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:34.169
to limit the risk of this network to be discovered
by authorities.

00:05:34.169 --> 00:05:43.210
But ultimately the person decides himself
or herself what is the level of risk that

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:48.110
they can tolerate in fighting this brutal
regime.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:54.230
Your organization has been clear that the
Russian people aren't simply going to overthrow

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.230
Putin.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.230
It's just not going to happen.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:01.880
So, so in the grand scheme of things, the
kind of resistance you're asking for: Can

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.020
that justify the risks you're asking people
to take?

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:14.560
I think the change in Russia will come from
a combination of dissatisfaction in the political

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:20.860
and business elite of Russia and the wide
discontent in the population.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:29.050
And both of these groups of people were having
a quite a hard time since the war started.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:36.199
People at the top have seen their fortunes
decimated, their lifestyles - when they can

00:06:36.199 --> 00:06:41.949
vacation in Western Europe, when their children
go to British private schools, when their

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:46.250
yachts are moored in Italy - has been shattered.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:53.530
And for an average person, they have seen
inflation, they have seen familiar foreign

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.850
brands leaving Russia.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:07:02.730
And now they see a constant stream of coffins
coming back from Ukraine.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.460
And for what?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:11.750
The military operation has not been going
very successfully for Russian army.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:19.389
So, these processes take time, but at some
point they will reinforce each other.

00:07:19.389 --> 00:07:24.069
And that's, I think, the only plausible scenario
for change.

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:28.660
You talk about people seeing coffins returning
from the war.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:33.870
People are also seeing hundreds put in jail,
many facing 15-year sentences for resisting

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.840
in the most trivial ways.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.410
Maybe they once gave money to an organization
like yours that's now banned.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.540
Police informers everywhere.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.750
Who knows how many may have penetrated your
organizations?

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:53.479
What's been the response to your call for
this "partisan underground"?

00:07:53.479 --> 00:08:06.310
We are basing our efforts on more than a decade
of work in Russia in different regions.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:18.909
Before the war started we had over 10 million
subscribers to different, different social

00:08:18.909 --> 00:08:23.600
networks that were broadcasting our message.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:31.260
We had an email distribution list of over
a million people.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:36.430
So, we are not starting from scratch.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:47.560
And obviously we, for understandable reasons,
we don't disclose the response and we don’t

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:52.910
disclose the scale of these activities.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:56.149
But we are quite optimistic.

00:08:56.149 --> 00:09:03.529
The response has been dozens of thousands
of people who would like to participate in

00:09:03.529 --> 00:09:04.529
this network.

00:09:04.529 --> 00:09:11.769
Mr. Ashurkov, one of your most ambitious ventures
has been to compile a list of 6000 Russians

00:09:11.769 --> 00:09:17.550
said to be bribe takers, warmongers, corrupt
officials, propagandists, people you accuse

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:21.040
of enabling the invasion of Ukraine.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.910
Are you not concerned that this is the equivalent
of sort of painting a target on their back

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:29.480
and encouraging people to shoot at them?

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:39.180
Indeed, there have been many people who are
the pillars of this regime.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:46.490
People who are involved in war propaganda,
people who are officials in various levels

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:53.880
of Russian government, businessmen connected
to Putin's regime, his cronies.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:10:05.130
And the-, for years our team has been advocating
sanctions, personal sanctions against perpetrators

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:09.250
of human rights abuses, against people involved
in corruption.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:13.750
But our calls have been falling on deaf ears.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:21.529
It has been a trickle in terms of sanctions,
even after the Russian annexation of Crimea

00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:24.450
and meddling in eastern Ukraine.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:35.320
Now, after the war, we've seen an avalanche
of sanctions and it was important for us to

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:43.060
make suggestions to Western governments to
make their sanctions policy more nuanced.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:53.820
And we came up with this list that we advocate
and we lobby various Western governments that

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.839
these people are included.

00:10:55.839 --> 00:11:05.350
They are people who have contributed to the
start of the war and who are now continuing

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:08.860
to support the war.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:22.570
That's-, that has been the sort of the premise
of our project, and it has received quite

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:31.760
good support from the governments in the EU,
in the US and the UK.

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:40.660
Just recently there was a resolution passed
in US House of Representatives calling for

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:50.459
the executive branch to review the 200 most
visible, the top priority 200 people from

00:11:50.459 --> 00:11:53.830
our list in terms of sanctioning them in the
US.

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.410
So I think it's working.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.923
One important aspect of our list is....

00:11:57.923 --> 00:11:59.450
I want to ask you- Yes, just...

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:00.450
Sure.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.329
Just, briefly just briefly.

00:12:02.329 --> 00:12:08.740
By September, five months after you went public,
there are only some 50 people on the list

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:12.540
who had contacted you and asked to be taken
off it.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.560
Are you surprised that the vast majority seemed
completely untroubled by your accusations

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.600
and just ignored the shaming?

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.260
The actual number is over 100...

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.899
Out of 6.000.
...and it's mostly...

00:12:26.899 --> 00:12:28.720
Out of 6.000.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.399
Out of, out of 6.000, indeed.

00:12:31.399 --> 00:12:32.450
It's not many, is it?

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:33.640
It's not many.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:42.519
To me, anything that's above zero-, If a person
changes his or her mind in terms of support

00:12:42.519 --> 00:12:50.350
of the war, in terms of being part of the
government structures, being on the board

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:57.209
of Russian state-owned companies, that's already
a lot because without our list, this number

00:12:57.209 --> 00:12:58.899
would be zero.

00:12:58.899 --> 00:13:01.760
So, it has been over 100.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:08.000
We are constantly reviewing this list.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.800
Every two weeks there are some updates.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:18.389
We take people out if there are reasons to
believe that they don't-, that they no longer

00:13:18.389 --> 00:13:19.889
qualify for being on the list.

00:13:19.889 --> 00:13:23.620
We make additions.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:34.340
And specifically the nature of our list is
that we want to use it not as much as an instrument

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:43.160
of punishment, but as an instrument of coercion
so that less people support the war and contribute

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.160
to it.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:49.820
So for instance, if we take Western sanctions,
it has been a one-way ticket.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:58.240
A person, an official or a businessman is
sanctioned and there is nothing they can do

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:00.760
that can remove them from this list.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:02.560
With us, it's different.

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:09.360
If you're on the board of a state company,
if you resign or if you are in the top management

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:17.680
of a state company, agency or organization
resign, send us proof of that and we'll review

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.910
it and we'll take you out.

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:20.910
So..

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:21.910
Okay.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.029
All right.
...our list is live.

00:14:24.029 --> 00:14:29.370
To date, you're the best-known opposition
group in Russia and you’ve had some remarkable

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:30.370
successes.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:35.810
You lifted the lid on a huge amount of corruption,
you've shown films, Putin's Palace, for instance.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:39.519
You've named names and reported on wide ranging
corruption.

00:14:39.519 --> 00:14:43.420
12 million views a month on YouTube, something
like that.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:49.769
But what sign is there that any of that has
materially affected Putin's support in the

00:14:49.769 --> 00:14:50.769
country?

00:14:50.769 --> 00:14:58.240
Navalny has said Putin is afraid of the truth,
but Putin simply shrugs off your truth as

00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.870
‘fake news’.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.149
What's he got to be afraid of?

00:15:03.149 --> 00:15:08.730
It's not easy to fight an oppressive regime
like Putin's.

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:11.889
We have been doing it for a number of years.

00:15:11.889 --> 00:15:17.680
There are some objective benchmarks how you
can judge a successful political movement.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:27.370
I think the most objective result was the
results of elections of Moscow mayor in 2013

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:32.100
when Alexei Navalny was able to participate.

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:35.399
That's sort of an objective measure, the results
of an election.

00:15:35.399 --> 00:15:42.920
So he got 28% of votes as opposed to 51 for
the incumbent mayor.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:50.410
So, and that was despite all the administrative
obstacles that we had, despite Navalny being

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:58.970
a sort of a newcomer, despite the incumbent
mayor having all the sources, all the resources

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:04.350
that the power was able to give him.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.350
So...

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.540
This was nine years ago.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.540
Mr. Ashurkov.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.540
I'm talking about now.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.329
Everything has changed since then.

00:16:10.329 --> 00:16:11.910
Everything has changed.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.069
What has Putin got to be afraid of now?

00:16:14.069 --> 00:16:18.630
Navalny is in jail and your organization is
banned and labelled extremist.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:20.120
What's he got to be afraid of?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:32.029
As I said, it will be the wide discontent
in population and the disillusionment with

00:16:32.029 --> 00:16:34.700
the regime in the elite.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:42.480
If you-, even if you talk about close circle
of Putin, they are really not happy with the

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.240
state of affairs.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:48.350
They are afraid of Putin and of his security
apparatus.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:54.830
But they, of course, would like to go back
to how things were and they were able to enjoy

00:16:54.830 --> 00:17:05.890
their wealth, they were integrated in the
West and they were able to enjoy the lifestyle

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:07.380
that they were used to.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.919
Now it's all broken.

00:17:10.919 --> 00:17:13.299
And that's what Putin needs to be afraid.

00:17:13.299 --> 00:17:20.400
There is a big factor, of course, what happens
on the battlefields of Ukraine.

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:21.400
And...

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.360
All right, I want to come to that.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.140
I want to come to that a little later.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:30.070
But I want to talk also about the opposition
movement in general in Russia.

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:35.510
And plenty of people have talked about the
disunity that seems to attend these groups.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:41.860
Why hasn't your organization put more effort
into improving relations with other opposition

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:42.860
groups?

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:46.370
After all, you share quite a few goals, don't
you, with each other?

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:54.650
Indeed, we have been working with various
democratic political forces for years.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:18:00.799
We created the Coordination Council in 2012.

00:18:00.799 --> 00:18:08.220
We participated in a number of elections together
with different other democratic forces...

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:11.169
But that didn't always work out, did it?

00:18:11.169 --> 00:18:14.950
I mean, it ended up-, you ended up squabbling
with other groups.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:27.630
I remember in 2021-, when was the last election,
2021, the opposition member Anastasia Bryukhanova,

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:34.289
she said the opposition can't be united, a
liberal can't agree with a nationalist or

00:18:34.289 --> 00:18:35.400
a communist.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.660
It's simply impossible.

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:41.809
It's a big drawback, this kind of disunity,
isn't it?

00:18:41.809 --> 00:18:42.850
Not really.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:55.220
The people who make real effort at trying
to do something useful and not just talk,

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:56.840
they achieve successes.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:19:00.120
We are in contact with various opposition
groups.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:10.640
But the thing that made Navalny and our organization
successful - and we increase our recognition

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:19.380
and we are able to create the regional networks
and we are able now to keep dozens of people

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:26.120
in our office outside of Russia - is that
we focus just on a few things.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:30.610
We do investigations, we do media work.

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:41.400
Our YouTube channels are probably the most
popular current news sources in Russia.

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:48.179
And now we're restoring this work in Russia
through our regional network.

00:19:48.179 --> 00:19:52.800
And we have a certain hierarchy.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:20:01.900
We have about 70 people, mostly in Vilnius,
in a few other European cities as well, who

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.909
work full-time on this.

00:20:03.909 --> 00:20:11.320
And for us to join forces with somebody, there
has to be a goal.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:15.150
The other parties need to bring something
to the table.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:26.429
It's not enough just to be a blogger with
50,000 followers to be able to join forces

00:20:26.429 --> 00:20:31.299
with us and to have equal voices in what we
do.

00:20:31.299 --> 00:20:37.200
Mr. Ashurkov, do you ever foresee a time when
Navalny or your group could possibly emerge

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:42.360
again as a serious political contender on
Russia's national stage?

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:48.770
I ask because Vladimir Milov, a former minister
and economic adviser to Navalny, said last

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:53.150
week that Russia's organized opposition is
destroyed.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:59.890
There is no mechanism, he said, for public
discontent to translate into political change.

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:02.120
Can you honestly tell me he's wrong?

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.760
Well, I think he's right...

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:08.200
He's one of your-, he's one of your closest
advisers.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.200
Absolutely.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:15.960
But you always need to put words in the context.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:25.770
Indeed, if you protest openly against the
war and against Putin's brutality in Russia,

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:32.690
you will be fined, you will be detained and
ultimately you will be jailed.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:33.690
That's the situation.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:42.360
So in this sense, organized opposition in
Russia that can participate in elections,

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:51.720
that can launch campaigns, they can-, that
can do organized mass protests - it's really

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:54.070
not possible at this point.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:22:01.940
But the millions of people who supported us,
who supported other democratic forces, many

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:07.730
of whom who had to move out of Russia, they
didn't go anywhere.

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:20.050
And once the political situation in Russia
change - a gradual liberalization and end

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:29.520
of hostilities with Ukraine and start of some
sort of communication with the West in a constructive

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:37.960
way - once that starts, and I believe that
it will start within the next five years,

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:46.299
maybe even earlier, I think there will be
a opening for us and for other democratic

00:22:46.299 --> 00:22:50.180
forces to enter the Russian politics properly
to...

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:57.130
If the war is as long and bitter as some people
fear, what do you think that will do to Russia?

00:22:57.130 --> 00:23:02.650
You've said you think there might be an end
to hostilities over the next five years.

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:08.760
Do you see any sign of deep and abiding changes
taking place in the country as a result of

00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:12.010
this war?

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:13.820
Different people believe in different things.

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:22.980
In terms of war, from where we sit today it's
difficult to envision that the war will end

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:25.030
in the next few months.

00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:33.240
I think it's something like a year, in a year
I think is a reasonable prediction that the

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:35.470
hostilities will stop.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:36.470
The...

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:37.470
Why?

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:38.470
Based on what?

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:40.920
What makes you say that?

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:54.240
I think within a year it's reasonable to expect
that Ukrainian army will make a few more significant

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:57.370
advances on the battlefield.

00:23:57.370 --> 00:24:05.860
We see that the Russian military capabilities
are deteriorating while Ukraine's capability

00:24:05.860 --> 00:24:11.870
and the flow of arms and coordination is improving.

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:22.000
They are already bold enough to launch attacks
in the sort of-, in the jewel of Russian Navy

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:26.770
in Sevastopol naval base in Crimea.

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:27.770
So I think the military...

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:32.580
And you think Russia is just going to give
up in the end and go home?

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:34.880
Militarily-, That's not what I said.

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:42.520
I'm saying that the military capabilities,
the balance of power is shifting to Ukraine,

00:24:42.520 --> 00:24:49.130
and we will see that manifesting itself on
the battlefield.

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:56.960
The economic sanctions placed on Russia will
be taking their gradual toll.

00:24:56.960 --> 00:25:09.740
The-, and of course, the losses from the Ukrainian
front are taking-, are affecting the mood

00:25:09.740 --> 00:25:12.720
of Russian public.

00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:21.929
So I think in a year these processes would
lead to possibly - and again, we're all speaking

00:25:21.929 --> 00:25:28.649
in probabilities and possibilities here - to
Russia's inability to continue the war.

00:25:28.649 --> 00:25:29.970
That's my prediction.

00:25:29.970 --> 00:25:30.970
Alright.

00:25:30.970 --> 00:25:33.130
Vladimir Ashurkov, it's been good to have
you on the program.

00:25:33.130 --> 00:25:35.230
Thank you very much indeed for being on Conflict
Zone.

00:25:35.230 --> 00:25:36.230
Thank you.

00:25:36.230 --> 00:25:37.230
Thank you for having me.

00:25:37.230 --> 00:25:37.650
Thank you.

